  "title": "Callback Pattern",
  "concept": "A callback is a function passed as an argument to another function, to be executed later",
  "content": {
    "code": "function processArray(arr, callback) {\n  const results = [];\n  for (let i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {\n    const processed = callback(arr[i], i);\n    results.push(processed);\n  }\n  return results;\n}\n\nfunction double(value, index) {\n  return value * 2;\n}\n\nfunction addIndex(value, index) {\n  return value + index;\n}\n\nconst numbers = [1, 2, 3];\nconst doubled = processArray(numbers, double);\nconst indexed = processArray(numbers, addIndex);\n\nconsole.log(doubled);\nconsole.log(indexed);",
